From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:46:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Boost the submit path by default

The time from a doorbell to the host noticing a completion is spent
largely on the CPU: the poll path, the wake-up of the scheduler work
and the retirement. With the CPU clusters at their idle clocks and the
scheduler work on a normal workqueue, that path is several times longer
than the GPU work of a small command.

Enable both bits of g16_submit_boost by default: queues run their
scheduler work on a high-priority ordered workqueue, and the CPU
clusters are held at their top frequency while commands are in flight.
The frequency request is released after the last command retires (with
the g16_lat_qos_us window), so an idle GPU does not hold the clocks.
g16_submit_boost=0 gives the previous behaviour.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index adfd063cfa..3a63ad7cbd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -952,8 +952,8 @@ pub(crate) fn clpc_demand() -> bool {
     "G16: report GPU work in flight to the CLPC, which raises the DRAM and fabric rails while it lasts (default 0: not reported; 1: reported; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_submit_boost` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static SUBMIT_BOOST: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_submit_boost` (runtime 0644, default 3).
+static SUBMIT_BOOST: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(3);
 
 /// Bit 0: queues created from now on run their scheduler work on a high-priority ordered
 /// workqueue. Bit 1: every cpufreq policy is held at its top frequency while commands are in
@@ -968,7 +968,7 @@ pub(crate) fn submit_boost() -> u32 {
     SUBMIT_BOOST_PARM,
     SUBMIT_BOOST,
     "g16_submit_boost",
-    "G16: bit 0: queues created from now on submit on a high-priority ordered workqueue; bit 1: hold the CPU clusters at their top frequency while commands are in flight, released at idle (default 0: off; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: bit 0: queues created from now on submit on a high-priority ordered workqueue; bit 1: hold the CPU clusters at their top frequency while commands are in flight, released at idle (default 3: both; 0: off; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_subgen` (runtime 0644, default 0).
